        "value": "ting the same evening. None of this is a crisis; it is an ordinary busy stretch, handled better than the last one, and the honest numbers show both the wobble and the recovery. The thing to watch is whether the routine survives two late nights in a row, which has not happened yet this month and would be the real test. If it does, that is worth saying out loud to him, because he is quicker to notice the misses than the saves.\n\nSmall wins this week:\n- six nights closed out on time\n- lunch away from the desk on three days\n- the phone out of the bedroom every night but one\n- one long walk outdoors on the weekend\n- the weekly review done on Sunday, not skipped\n- a call with a friend, the first in a while\n\nLooking ahead: the end-of-month deadline lands next week, so the evenings will be tight. The plan is a fixed stop time on the two heaviest days, a walk before work instead of after, and the weekly review moved to Saturday morning so Sunday stays free.\n"
