        "name": "📝 Week notes · 4",
        "value": "A note on the numbers: only two days were logged this week, which reads worse than the week felt. The logging slipped on the busy days, not the routine itself, and the two are easy to confuse from the outside. Getting the daily log back to every day is the one change he picked for next week, and a friendly nudge on Wednesday or Thursday, when it usually slips, would help it stick.\n\nWhat went well: six of seven nights closed out, the morning routine held on the workdays, and he kept the weekly review even after a rough Wednesday.\n\nWhat he's carrying: a deadline at the end of the month, a schedule with very little slack, and the worry that one late meeting can undo a good week.\n\nWhat would help: a short message midweek, an invitation to something outdoors on the weekend, and asking him how the new routine is landing rather than how the numbers look."
